From: Marionette <marionette@localhost>
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] mute the latched beacon-miss indication during AWDL capture

Patch 0049 made capture_hold=0 actually reset the monitor filters, and that
part works: dmesg shows

	MARIONETTE_STA_NORMAL_RX_RESTORED status=0 monitor=0

and station RX keeps moving after the release.  The link still dies anyway.

Measured 2026-10-23, station associated to 70:3a:73:a2:26:68 on 5260, one
resident monitor vdev, never deleted:

| shape                                  | result                                  |
|----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
| hold 2 s once, then released for 60 s  | rxbytes 105748 -> 119214 over 13 s, then |
|                                        | disconnect at t=15 s, 3 bmiss events    |
| hold 2 s / release 3 s, 60 s loop      | disconnect at t=15 s, assert_delta=0    |
| hold 200 ms / release 800 ms, 60 s     | disconnect at t=12 s, assert_delta=0    |

The 200 ms shape is the giveaway.  If the miss counter were a per-beacon count
that a good beacon reset, a 200 ms hold would never accumulate enough misses
to trip.  It dies at the same ~12-15 s as the 2 s shape, so the indication is
latched in the firmware the first time the filters are installed and fires on
its own schedule afterwards, regardless of how much beacon traffic flows in
between.

The chain is:

	wmi event -> wma_beacon_miss_handler()            (core/wma/src/wma_mgmt.c)
	          -> WMA_MISSED_BEACON_IND
	          -> lim_ps_offload_handle_missed_beacon_ind()   "Received Heart Beat Failure"
	          -> lim_send_heart_beat_timeout_ind()
	          -> AP probing -> QCA_DISCONNECT_REASON_BEACON_MISS_FAILURE

Every step after the first is host-side policy.  This patch drops the
indication at the first host boundary, before the netif queues are stopped and
before PE starts probing, so the station stays associated and data keeps
flowing for the whole capture session.

The mute is a writable module parameter rather than an unconditional behaviour,
because it does hide a real link loss.  radio.sh is expected to set it while
the resident capture runs, check real traffic during the release gaps, and
clear it if the link is genuinely gone.

	/sys/module/kiwi_v2/parameters/marionette_awdl_bmiss_mute

If this holds, the resident design needs no vdev churn and no asserts: one
monitor vdev opened once, filters toggled, beacon-miss muted for the duration.

--- a/platform/inc/marionette_sta_monitor.h
+++ b/platform/inc/marionette_sta_monitor.h
@@ -5,4 +5,5 @@
 bool marionette_sta_monitor_enabled(void);
 bool marionette_sta_monitor_capture_enabled(void);
 int marionette_monitor_refresh_filters(void *soc_handle, bool hold);
+bool marionette_bmiss_mute_enabled(void);
 #endif
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_main.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_main.c
@@ -20176,8 +20176,44 @@
 		"Hold the capture RX filters on without moving the channel; "
 		"pair with a remain-on-channel reservation");
 
+/* Mute the firmware beacon-miss indication while the resident AWDL capture
+ * owns the receive ring.
+ *
+ * Holding the monitor filters diverts beacons away from the station, so the
+ * firmware raises a missed-beacon indication and PE drops the link about 13 s
+ * later -- even after the filters are released and beacons are flowing again.
+ * Measured 2026-10-23 with a single 2 s hold: station RX kept moving for 13 s
+ * (105748 -> 119214 bytes) and then went down with
+ * QCA_DISCONNECT_REASON_BEACON_MISS_FAILURE.  The indication is latched, so
+ * releasing the filters cannot cancel it, and neither a 2 s nor a 200 ms
+ * capture window changes the outcome: both shapes died ~12-15 s after the
+ * first hold.
+ *
+ * Dropping the indication at the WMA boundary keeps the link up for the whole
+ * capture session.  Liveness is then the service's job: radio.sh checks real
+ * traffic while the filters are released and lifts the mute if the link is
+ * genuinely gone.
+ */
+static bool marionette_awdl_bmiss_mute;
+
+bool marionette_bmiss_mute_enabled(void)
+{
+	return READ_ONCE(marionette_awdl_bmiss_mute);
+}
+
+static const struct kernel_param_ops marionette_bmiss_mute_ops = {
+	.set = param_set_bool,
+	.get = param_get_bool,
+};
+
+module_param_cb(marionette_awdl_bmiss_mute, &marionette_bmiss_mute_ops,
+		&marionette_awdl_bmiss_mute, 0600);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(marionette_awdl_bmiss_mute,
+		"Drop firmware beacon-miss indications while the AWDL capture ring is held");
+
 #else
 bool marionette_sta_monitor_capture_enabled(void) { return false; }
+bool marionette_bmiss_mute_enabled(void) { return false; }
 #endif
 
 module_param_cb(con_mode, &con_mode_ops, &con_mode,
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/wma/src/wma_mgmt.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/wma/src/wma_mgmt.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 /* Header files */
 
 #include "marionette_awdl_rx_diagnostics.h"
+#include "marionette_sta_monitor.h"
 #include "wma.h"
 #include "wma_api.h"
 #include "cds_api.h"
@@ -2641,6 +2642,17 @@
 	struct missed_beacon_ind *beacon_miss_ind;
 	struct mac_context *mac = cds_get_context(QDF_MODULE_ID_PE);
 
+	/* The resident AWDL capture diverts beacons, so the firmware reports a
+	 * miss that is an artefact of the experiment rather than a dead link.
+	 * The indication is latched in the firmware: once raised it disconnects
+	 * the station ~13 s later no matter how quickly the filters are
+	 * released.  Drop it here, before the netif queues are stopped and
+	 * before PE starts AP probing, so traffic keeps flowing. */
+	if (marionette_bmiss_mute_enabled()) {
+		wma_info("MARIONETTE_BMISS_MUTED vdev=%d rssi=%d", vdev_id, rssi);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	beacon_miss_ind = qdf_mem_malloc(sizeof(*beacon_miss_ind));
 	if (!beacon_miss_ind)
 		return;
